  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Agora Theater in Cleveland, Ohio, on Friday, September 26, 2025 [1]. This event is the 438th archived show in the Internet Archive’s collection for the band, following a previous performance at Thompson’s Point on August 9, 2025 [2]. The only available recording is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones, captured and transferred by Tape&Bake, running for 99 minutes [1]. The setlist includes rare and first-in-archive tracks such as “New Britain,” “Hatha Hill,” and “Great Pirates” [1]. Notable bustouts include “Ice Cream, Cobra Man,” which had not been played in 239 archived shows, and “Warewolf Gimmick,” absent from 144 prior recordings [1]. The band also performed “Bones Don’t Rust” and “We Were Patriots,” both of which have limited archive presence [1]. The performance features spoken introductions and stories, including one about “No Children” and band wrestling [1]. This recording offers a complete view of the evening’s repertoire, spanning albums from “Full Force Galesburg” to “Dark in Here” [1].",
